    <p class="tag">Specialised Service</p>
    <h1>Your Situation Doesn't Always Fit Neatly Into One Category</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Our assistance doesn't have to either.</p>

    <p>Not every immigration situation is a single, straightforward transaction. Some involve several issues at once: different visas, statuses, records or requirements that interact with one another. Foreign Immigration Services reviews the full picture and puts together a coordinated plan, rather than treating a complex situation as though it were one standard service.</p>

    <div class="proposition-highlight">
      <h2>One Strategy for the Whole Immigration Picture</h2>
      <p>When several immigration issues affect one another, solving them one at a time can create more problems than it resolves. FIS assesses the situation as a whole, determines what needs to happen and in what order, and coordinates the required immigration work through one tailored strategy.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Situations in Which This Service May Be Appropriate</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You are dealing with more than one immigration issue at the same time</li>
      <li>Your circumstances are unusual and don't map cleanly onto a single standard service</li>
      <li>Resolving one issue may depend on addressing another one first</li>
      <li>You know something needs to be sorted out, but you're not sure which issue to address first</li>
      <li>Your situation involves a mix of visa, status, documentation and compliance concerns</li>
      <li>You need a tailored sequence of applications, documentation, liaison or coordination handled together, rather than as one-off requests</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Assessing your immigration circumstances as a whole and identifying the issues that need to be addressed</li>
      <li>Determining how the different immigration issues affect one another and what should be addressed first</li>
      <li>Developing a tailored strategy for the applications, regularisation, documentation or other immigration work required</li>
      <li>Preparing and organising the relevant applications and supporting documentation</li>
      <li>Managing and coordinating connected immigration transactions, rather than requiring you to handle each one separately</li>
      <li>Liaising with the Bureau of Immigration and other relevant authorities on your behalf</li>
      <li>Following through on each stage and adapting the plan as connected matters progress</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Initial enquiry</h3>
        <p>Tell us what's going on, in as much or as little detail as you have.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Holistic assessment</h3>
        <p>We review your overall situation and identify the immigration issues involved.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Prioritisation</h3>
        <p>We work out how those issues interact and what needs to be addressed first.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Tailored assistance plan</h3>
        <p>We put together a coordinated plan suited to your specific circumstances.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Coordinated assistance</h3>
        <p>We carry out and coordinate the relevant applications, documentation and immigration processes, keeping you updated as the matter progresses. You can track the progress of your transactions through the FIS Client Portal.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What We May Need From You</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your passport and other identity information</li>
      <li>Any existing immigration documents you have, such as visas, your ACR I-Card, or previous applications</li>
      <li>Correspondence or notices you have received from the Bureau of Immigration or other relevant authorities, if any</li>
      <li>A general history of your travel and immigration status in the Philippines</li>
      <li>A description of your situation in your own words. We will help make sense of the details</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="service-cta">
      <h2>Dealing With More Than One Immigration Issue?</h2>
      <p>Tell us what's happening. FIS can assess the full picture, determine what needs to be addressed and in what order, and coordinate the immigration work required to move the matter forward.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?service=complex-tailored">Discuss Your Situation</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>How is this different from your other services?</summary>
        <p>Most of our other services are designed around a particular immigration need or type of process. Complex &amp; Tailored Immigration Assistance is for circumstances involving multiple interconnected issues, or situations that do not fit neatly within a single service category. We assess the broader picture, determine how the different issues interact and coordinate the appropriate immigration work accordingly.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I'm not sure if my situation is "complex" enough for this. Should I still get in touch?</summary>
        <p>Yes. You do not need to determine the right service before contacting us. Tell us what is happening and FIS can assess the situation, identify the issues involved and determine the appropriate way to handle them.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can FIS handle several connected immigration matters at the same time?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Where your circumstances involve several connected immigration matters, FIS can assess how they interact, determine the appropriate sequence and coordinate the relevant transactions as part of one tailored engagement.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

